CERT Polska's advisory names the vendor, the products and the affected ranges and says nothing about where DHTMLX components are deployed, so the claim that they are widely embedded in EU e-government, healthcare scheduling and municipal planning tools has no source ([CERT Polska, 2026-05-15](https://cert.pl/en/posts/2026/05/CVE-2026-7182/)). The disclosure covers the PDF Export Module used by DHTMLX Gantt and Scheduler and the export module of DHTMLX Diagram, not the scheduling and diagram libraries as a whole ([CERT Polska, 2026-05-15](https://cert.pl/en/posts/2026/05/CVE-2026-7182/)). CVE-2026-41552 and CVE-2026-7182 are path-traversal flaws that let crafted HTML include local server files in the generated PDF rather than code execution, with CVSS 4.0 scores of 9.2 ([ENISA EUVD-2026-30538](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/enisa/eu_vulnerability_database/EUVD-2026-30538); [ENISA EUVD-2026-30539](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/enisa/eu_vulnerability_database/EUVD-2026-30539)). The PDF Export Module is affected from release 0.3.3 and fixed in 0.7.6, and Diagram from 1.0.0 and fixed in 1.1.1 ([ENISA EUVD-2026-30537](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/enisa/eu_vulnerability_database/EUVD-2026-30537); [CERT Polska, 2026-05-15](https://cert.pl/en/posts/2026/05/CVE-2026-7182/)). The EPSS score of 0.39 given earlier was not supported, and the score is not carried here.
